ginning to look past at sell by  date the design department kicked around  various ideas until head designer Bill  Mitchell got inspiration for the first  Corvette Coupe a from an actual stingray  the new stingray was even sporty-er  leaner and meaner  47 year-old engineer Oliver leap is a  Corvette fan body and soul he collects  everything connected with this  automotive icon his impressive  collection includes Corvettes from 1964  to 1996 but his favorite is the c2 the  Stingray model built from 1963 to 67  whenever he finds some time in his busy  schedule he takes one of his treasures  out for a spin  he says he dreamt of Corvettes even as a  child he saw one as a small boy and  immediately fell in love with it  eventually he began collecting them  whenever he could he admits it's a  typical male dream  he explains that in American car  collector circles the c2 is the USA's  answer to the Porsche it handles very  well in comparison to its contemporaries  and relative to other vintage classic  sports cars it's still affordable over  tribe have his blue 65 coupe a  completely restored and customized to  his own specifications in the United  States but Corvette fan though he is he  says the performance of the big-block v8  is only just enough  American car fans call a Corvette like  Oliver's a sleeper that means it has  lots of power under the hood but  everything else is like the original  nowadays a stingray in good condition  can run a good 50 thousand euros the  most sought-after models are the big  blocks and split-window coupe A's  the best place to find one ethanol is in  the United States
 

